Here's our local squable spilling over into eff.talk which it has done
intermittently.  Let's get the rest of the world up to speed here.  We
may need all the help we can get.

First and foremost, NOTHING illegal has gone on in either the Nyx or the
newsgroup alt.sex.intergen-  A nyxin, Tim Hester, is ranting that Nyx SysOp
Andrew Burt censor a.s.i-  His subject heading raves, "Usenet AIDS In
Victimizing Children".  Hester has threatened to have his article of        
chimerical contention, with it's proposal of an unconstitutional solution
published in the Denver Post.

Burt seemed overly nervous about this for a man who's philosophy of Public
Access and eloquence on the subject of Free Speech is patent.  Nyx hangs by
a T1 thread to the internet by the good gracesf the Denver University 
Math/CS Dept.  TCI is a major contributer to DU.  DU views Nyx as a potential
liability and notes that Nyx generates no income for DU.  Andrew Burt fears
that this may be the straw that breaks the camel's back.

Tim Hester does not write.  He types.  We all seriously doubted he would
convince a responsible editor to publish him.  At noon Friday, a message
was left in Andrew Burt's office to return the call of a Denver Post reporter.
Burt got the message at 6 PM MST and the reporter had left for the weekend.
Several Rocky Mountain News reporters are Nyx users.  This is the rival 
publication of the Denver Post.  However, Andrew fee that another ta  
on the Nyx in the Denver press would ill bode the DU Chancelory toward Nyx.
Perhaps to the point of pulling the plug.

Simply put, Hester does not like what the subscribers to alt.sex.intergen
have to say.  He wants them censored.  He is trying to raise as much hell
as he can over the issue, and has caught Burt in a precarious position.

John, if you're reading this, could you please respond?  We all know that
we need Clipper Chips so the government can protect us from kiddie porn;)
The ambiguity of international law comes into play as the age of consent is
much lower in many European countries.  The subscribers of alt.sex.intergen
are talking- not posting GIF's.  One electronic community of 10,000 hangs
in the balance.  This is right up your alley, and I'd be very interested
to hear what you have to say about this issue. 

