hello, my school, the University of Scranton, is currently undergoing a 
censorship crisis.  Scince this is newsgroup about censorship i decided
to post here and hopefully get some responses that i could use to write
a paper with.
	here is the situation:  over christmas break, the administrator
of our SUN systems which are the only computers here directly linked to
NEWS, decided that he would not subscibe to some NEWS groups that he found
offensive (i do not have any exact names).  He talked to the computer 
science departement and ask their permision to unsubscribe to the alleged
groups and (from what i have heard) they said it was up to his own judgement
(which to me means that they gave him permision).  after a while, someone
noticed that his NEWS group was gone, and it was one of those groups where
they post pornography.  I am not too sure exactly how things happened next
but in the end the person got about 60 people to write to the administrator
asking him why he took the stuff off.  (incedently, most of the NEWs readers
have accounts on our VAX system here which gets its news from the SUNs).
the administrator responded, and in some of them said that he felt it was
his right to censor the newsgroups because they were "ramming their opinions
