Now I get folks complaining about free speech, e.g.:

>+>Let Detweiler speak.

This is not a free speech issue.

I did not censor Mr. Detweiler for his views.  I simply refused to deal
with the negative feedback he had been generating.  His activities had
a significant impact on my workload, requiring me to respond to various
(questionable and usually frivolous) claims of abuse.  I'll blow off
a few net.whiners, but when complaints arrive daily I can't simply
ignore them.

Mr. Detweiler is no longer associated with this University except for
having received his undergraduate degree here in May, 1993.  His account
was kept active after his graduation as an extension service.  As such,
he was a guest using the facilities paid for by State funding and by
fees from currently enrolled students.  Had Mr.  Detweiler been a faculty
member, enrolled student, or had any other significant relationship with
the University, I might have been more inclined to champion his cause.
But he was not, and my limited resources were not willing to tolerate
the additional burden.

I maintain systems to support academic programs.  Other use is permitted
if it does not interfere with academic work.  The feedback from Detweiler's
activities was deemed to be interfering.  Does this make me a tyrant?  I
think not.

